From daa1cd895416ef580065ea7f0c6b9a757d2725cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:21:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] panvk/jm: v6/v7 tess draws share a batch: per-draw charge
 capped

Rationale: perf review 2026-10-26, finding D1. jm-v7 106 (0079) charges
each tessellated draw the worst case of its tess eval varyings against the
per-batch budget (PANVK_V7_TESS_BATCH_MB, 32 MiB): max_indices is bounded
by PANVK_TESS_MAX_PRIMS_PER_PATCH (level 64), so a 16-patch triangle draw
is charged 16 x 8704 x 3 indices x 54 B = 21.5 MiB. The second tess draw
of a batch is always over budget ("varyings 43 MiB worst case" in the 113
S9 and A31 logcats), so every tessellated draw got its own batch, two
atoms and a fragment job, and every batch after the first in a render pass
stores and reloads the whole framebuffer. PanProbe tess_perf records 256
batches (512 atoms) per frame; on 1080p game content each extra split is
about 15-33 MB of attachment traffic (2-4 ms on G52/G72). Real draws use a
small part of the charge: 27,744 indices (1.4 MiB) at level 16, 96 at
level 1.

Each draw is now charged at most budget / PANVK_V7_TESS_BATCH_DRAWS
(default 4), so four worst-case draws share a batch. Correctness does not
depend on the charge: panlib_v7_tess_prefix() keeps only the whole patches
whose varyings fit what is left of the batch's indirect varying buffer
(4M x 72 B of VA per heap half), and several tess draws per batch were
already recorded whenever their worst cases fit (small patch counts,
nested draws): they serialize through the tess arena with barrier jobs as
before. What changes is the memory a batch may touch: up to N x 21.5 MiB
of the GROW_ON_GPF varying buffer per half (86 MiB at N=4) when every
patch of every draw really reaches level 64, instead of 32 MiB; typical
content stays at N x 1-2 MiB. The GS scratch budget of nested draws is
unchanged. The "tess batch budget" log line now prints the charge and N.

Knob: PANVK_V7_TESS_BATCH_DRAWS (0-64, default 4; 0 = the whole worst case
per draw, 114). Read once per VkDevice into panvk_device::jm_opt.
PANVK_V7_TESS_BATCH_MB=0 still removes the budget. Arch: v6/v7.

Expected: tess_perf 64 instead of 256 batches per frame (L=1 should gain
most, its frame is mostly per-batch overhead); hashes unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device.h         |  3 +++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c      |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index 9b20e9c3..310c1893 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -3837,10 +3837,24 @@ panvk_tess_draw(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
     * phases of this draw.
     */
    const uint64_t tess_budget = panvk_v7_tess_batch_budget();
-   const uint64_t vary_w =
+   uint64_t vary_w =
       (uint64_t)max_indices * layers *
          (16 + 4 + tes_v->info.varyings.formats.generic_size_B) +
       (uint64_t)layers * 3 * 64;
+   /* The worst case is every patch at level 64 (PANVK_TESS_MAX_PRIMS_PER_
+    * PATCH): 21.5 MiB for a 16-patch triangle draw, so with the whole worst
+    * case charged every tess draw started a new batch, and every batch
+    * after the first in a render pass stores and reloads the framebuffer.
+    * Real draws use a small part of it (1.4 MiB at level 16). Each draw is
+    * charged at most budget / PANVK_V7_TESS_BATCH_DRAWS (default 4), so
+    * that many share a batch. The prefix kernel still keeps only the
+    * patches whose varyings fit what is left of the indirect varying
+    * buffer, so a batch that really reaches the worst case only takes
+    * more of that buffer (up to N times 21.5 MiB). 0 = the whole worst
+    * case (old).
+    */
+   if (tess_budget && dev->jm_opt.tess_batch_draws)
+      vary_w = MIN2(vary_w, tess_budget / dev->jm_opt.tess_batch_draws);
    if (!draw->indirect_dep_job && tess_budget) {
       struct panvk_batch *b = cmdbuf->cur_batch;
       const bool used = b->tess_vary_w || b->tess_gs_off;
@@ -3853,9 +3867,11 @@ panvk_tess_draw(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
          if (over && logged < 3) {
             logged++;
             mesa_logi("panvk: v%u tess batch budget %llu MiB: new batch "
-                      "(varyings %llu MiB worst case, GS scratch %llu MiB)",
+                      "(varyings %llu MiB charged, %u draws per batch, "
+                      "GS scratch %llu MiB)",
                       PAN_ARCH, (unsigned long long)(tess_budget >> 20),
                       (unsigned long long)((b->tess_vary_w + vary_w) >> 20),
+                      dev->jm_opt.tess_batch_draws,
                       (unsigned long long)(b->tess_gs_off >> 20));
          }
          panvk_per_arch(cmd_close_batch)(cmdbuf);
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device.h
index 3de854bc..46c56dc6 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device.h
@@ -93,6 +93,9 @@ struct panvk_device {
       /* PANVK_JM_RESET_FLUSH (default once, batch/0 = old): a resubmitted
        * command buffer cleans its descriptor pool once, not per batch. */
       bool reset_flush_once;
+      /* PANVK_V7_TESS_BATCH_DRAWS (default 4, 0 = old): v6/v7 tess draws
+       * that may share a batch at their worst-case varying charge. */
+      uint32_t tess_batch_draws;
    } jm_opt;
    struct panvk_priv_bo *sample_positions;
 
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
index 31716611..9ebb09c8 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
@@ -904,6 +904,8 @@ panvk_per_arch(create_device)(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device,
    /* v6/v7 panvk_tess_draw() reads it per draw (v9+ sets it below). */
    device->tess_opt.winding_inline =
       debug_get_num_option("PANVK_TESS_WINDING_INLINE", 1) != 0;
+   device->jm_opt.tess_batch_draws =
+      CLAMP(debug_get_num_option("PANVK_V7_TESS_BATCH_DRAWS", 4), 0, 64);
 #endif
 
 #if PAN_ARCH >= 9
-- 
